==Russian==
{{wp|ru:+ (значения)}}
[[Image:Sheep's face, Malta.jpg|thumb|Бирка на ухе овцы]]

===Etymology===
Unclear. There are several hypotheses:

# a borrowing from a {{der|ru|gmq}} word relating to commerce (stemming from [[birch]]): see {{cog|non|birk}} ({{m|non|biærk}}, {{m|non|berck}}, {{m|non|byrck}}), {{m|non|birki}}, {{m|non|birka||commerce hub}} ({{cog|non-oen|biærkø}}, {{cog|non-own|bjarkey}}, {{cog|fi|pirkka}}); see also {{cog|gmq-osw|birkarl}}, {{cog|fi|pirkkalaiset||mechant}}
# a {{der|ru|trk}} borrowing, compare to {{cog|tr|[[bir]] + [[iki]]||one + two}}
# a derivation from {{der|ru|orv|събьрати||to assemble}} (modern {{cog|ru|собира́ть}}), from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*bьrati||to take}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|би́рка}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|би́рка|*}}

# [[nameplate]], [[label]], [[tag]]
#: {{syn|ru|ярлы́к}}
